  #line-at(90.024pt, 151.22pt, "The hard breakdown voltage of the trench JBSDs ranged from 1.8-2kV, while the planar ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 178.82pt, "SBDs and HJDs showed significantly lower breakdown voltages of 566V and 948V, ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 206.42pt, "respectively. This shows the effectiveness of the trench design and the SM-JTE compared ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 234.02pt, "to that of the planar devices without edge termination. The optical images of the devices ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 261.65pt, "pre-breakdown and post-breakdown are shown in Fig. 5 (b), (c), respectively. Most ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 289.25pt, "devices broke down due to high electric fields at the trench-corner or at the edge of the ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 316.85pt, "SM-JTE edge termination (discussed later). The trench width of the JBSDs showed no ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 344.45pt, "significant impact on the breakdown voltage as shown in Fig. 5 (a). This is likely due to ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 372.05pt, "the breakdown occurring at the trench corners where the peak field only shows a ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 399.65pt, "marginal increase with increasing fin width (Fig. 6 (b)) or at the edge of the SM-JTE, ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 427.27pt, "where the field is independent of the fin width. Furthermore, from the TEM images we ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 454.87pt, "observe PR residue at the trench corners (between the metal and NiO) which likely also ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 482.47pt, "compromised the breakdown field of the NiO/Ga")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 8.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(336.19pt, 483.43pt, "2")
